## Air-family HID protocol (measured facts + community cross-verified 2026-11-14)

- Air, Air 2, **Air 2 Pro** speak the same protocol. Air 2 **Ultra** differs
  (IMU on interface 2, 512-byte packets) — exclude PID `0x0426`.
- **IMU = interface 3** (64-byte interrupt IN+OUT; commands, echoes, and
  sensor frames all on this one interface). **MCU = interface 4**
  (brightness/display/serial — never needed for pose). Interface 5 is
  undocumented by any community source; leave unclaimed. Interface 6 is the
  buttons as a standard 3-byte HID keyboard. Air 1 endpoint addresses are
  `0x84/0x05` (IMU) and `0x86/0x07` (MCU). This Air 2 Pro logged the same
  IMU pair on 2026-11-14: `endpoints in=132 out=5` (`0x84`/`0x05`).
- Command frame, little-endian, interrupt OUT write (no report-id prefix
  on Android raw USB; Windows hidapi needs a leading `0x00` — OS artifact):

  `[0]=0xAA · [1..4]=CRC-32 LE (zlib `java.util.zip.CRC32`) over bytes [5..end] · [5..6]=u16 length = 3+len(data) · [7]=msgid · [8..]=data`

- Start stream: msgid `0x19`, data `01` —
  `AA C5 D1 21 42 04 00 19 01` (captured ground truth in XrealBeam and
  AirAPI_Windows). Stop: msgid `0x19` data `00` —
  `AA 53 E1 26 35 04 00 19 00`. A single START write streams on Air 1;
  a stop→start pair is the belt-and-braces fallback.
- The device echoes **every** IMU command with one 64-byte reply on IN
  (echo head `AA`, msgid echoed). The START reply is often the INIT frame
  `AA 53 …` instead of an echo. The first command after open can time out
  — tolerate an unanswered first write.
- Sensor report (64-byte IN): head `01 02` (INIT is `AA 53`); u64 LE
  timestamp at `0x04`; gyro = i16 LE multiplier + i32 LE divisor + three
  i24 LE at `0x12/0x15/0x18` (**deg/s**, `value = raw*mult/div`);
  accel = mult/div at `0x1B/0x1D` + three i24 LE at `0x21/0x24/0x27`
  (**g**, +1 g along the body axis pointing up at rest); mag block is
  big-endian with an offset-encoding (`b0 | ((b1 ^ 0x80) << 8)`);
  CRC-32 at offset 54 that no community driver verifies — safe to ignore
  on read. No quaternion, no Euler: fusion is host-side.
- Sensor body axes are x left, y back, z up. Head/viewer axes
  (x right, y up, z back) = **(−x, z, y)**.
- Rate: nominal 1000 Hz; Android-measured 489–665 Hz on Air 1. This Air 2
  Pro (2026-11-14, SM-S948B): `timestamp=ns`, `pose-rate=991.4Hz`, one
  START `wrote=9`, no stop→start retry. Derive dt from the on-report u64
  timestamp; nominal ns but some firmware emits µs (runtime-detect: first
  sane delta < 50,000 ⇒ µs); drop Δ ≤ 0 or ≥ 0.5 s; 24-bit tick-rollover
  guard. Never assume a fixed rate.
- Yaw drift expectation: ~0.04–0.07°/min warm with bias handling,
  ~3°/min cold — a stationary gyro-bias estimator is required. The factory
  calibration blob (msgid `0x14`/`0x15`, ~38 KB JSON on Air 1) is optional;
  the stream runs without draining it.
- Android specifics: `claimInterface(3, force=true)` to detach the kernel
  `usbhid` driver; USB permission is revoked on replug (re-ask);
  XrealBeam used a `controlTransfer(0x21, 0x09, 0x0200, iface)` SET_REPORT
  fallback when an interface lacks an OUT endpoint — our dump shows
  interface 3 has one, so the interrupt OUT write is primary.
- No firmware gating on the Air family (the SDK-version/heartbeat handshake
  is XBX-only, PIDs `0x0440/0x0442`). Air PIDs: Air `0x0424`, Air 2
  `0x0428`, **Air 2 Pro `0x0432`**, Ultra `0x0426` (different protocol).

## One-series TCP — reference (not the owned unit)

### Device facts

- XREAL One: 1080p/eye, 50° diagonal FOV (~44°H × 26°V), ~42 ppd; One Pro:
  57° diagonal. 2D = 1920×1080 (120 Hz max, phone hosts typically 60 Hz);
  Full SBS = 3840×1080 @ 60 (we never drive SBS — 2D only).
- On-glasses X1 chip offers Anchor (3DoF world-lock) / Follow / Sideview via
  physical buttons. **No published host API** for anchor/recenter; the
  reverse-engineered command table (verified firmware 1.8.1) has **no
  anchor/follow/recenter opcode**. XREAL's own recenter = long-press X button.
- Sensor + control ride a **USB network interface** on the same USB-C link:
  link-local TCP `169.254.2.1:52998` (sensor stream: gyro/accel/mag, 128-byte
  reports) and `:52999` (control). No `UsbManager` permission dialog needed;
  requires `INTERNET` + `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE` and routing via the correct
  `Network` (`Network.socketFactory`) — plain `Socket()` will fail.
- XREAL One must sit in **Follow + Stabilizer off** for host-side XR mode:
  Anchor while the host also transforms = content moves twice / cut off;
  Stabilizer on = lag then glide-back. Misconfiguration is detectable via
  the panel-duty heuristic (panel duty ~90% = head-lock, ≤40% likely Anchor).
- XREAL glasses report **no DPI** to Android → desktop defaults to ~30 dpi;
  Dextop's density override handles it.
- Official native Android SDK does not exist (Unity-only; Enterprise SDK
  undocumented) — community TCP protocol is the only FOSS path.
- Owned pair verified 2026-11-14 on SM-S948B: **XREAL Air 2 Pro**, not One.
  EDID name `Air 2 Pro`, PNP `MRG`, product id 12597, week 8 / 2023.
  Panel 1920×1080 @ 60/90/120, dpi placeholder 25.4, HDR max 500 nits.
  USB VID **0x3318**, PID **0x0432**, manufacturer `XREAL`, product
  `XREAL Air 2 Pro`, serial `A00015:28:15`. Interfaces: 0–2 USB audio,
  3–5 HID 64-byte interrupt in+out, 6 HID in-only 3-byte. **No**
  `169.254.2.*` NIC — One TCP (`:52998`) does not apply to this unit.
  Card match is the vendor id, not the string and not this PID. Other
  models stay `xreal`; the adapter picks HID vs TCP from NIC presence.
  Device filter includes vendor `13080`. Grant completed 2026-11-14 18:30
  Africa/Addis_Ababa after the dialog was accepted on the phone screen
  (it had opened on display 0 while that panel was off). Stationary fused
  pose before Recenter: yaw −0.527, pitch 0.227, roll 2.711 rad. Head-turn
  signs and the Recenter press were not captured.

## Known control commands (One-series TCP, community, firmware 1.8.1)

- 2D↔SBS: `0x2822` (0 regular / 1 SBS) — causes video-mode blink + EDID re-advertise.
- Brightness: `0x271C` (0–9); electrochromic dimmer: `0x2727`;
  scene mode `0x2829` (hand glasses buttons to host); panel duty read `10065`.
- Firmware/serial queries, factory config JSON (IMU/display calibration).
- **Firmware OTAs can break the protocol** — version-gate on connect, fail
  soft to generic external display.

## Invariants

- Never rely on built-in Anchor for XR-mode content (double transform). On
  Air glasses this is moot: no glasses-side spatial chip exists at all.
- Never toggle SBS from Dextop (decision: 2D only).
- Air: USB permission is revoked on replug — re-ask through the card, never
  from a poll loop. One TCP: socket must come from the USB NIC's
  `Network.socketFactory`, not the default.
- Air: dt comes from the on-report timestamp, never a fixed rate. This
  unit is ns at 991.4 Hz; do not reuse the Viture 62.8 Hz clock.

## Symptom / cause / fix skeleton

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Air: no sensor frames after START | First write after open can go unanswered | Send stop→start once. This Air 2 Pro answered the first START (`wrote=9`); keep the one retry for firmware that does not |
| Air: replies seem shifted by one command | Every IMU command gets an echo; unread echoes pile up | Read one reply per write; INIT frame `AA 53` counts as the START reply |
| Air: yaw crawls while head is still | Gyro bias not estimated | Stationary-bias estimator at fusion start; recenter button for the user |
| Air: pose jumps wildly | Timestamp unit is µs on some firmware, treated as ns | Runtime-detect unit from first sane delta; drop Δ ≤ 0 or ≥ 0.5 s |
| TCP connect to 169.254.2.1 times out | Default network used instead of USB NIC `Network` | Enumerate `ConnectivityManager` networks; bind sockets via `Network.socketFactory` |
| Content moves twice as fast as head | Glasses in Anchor while host transforms | Onboard to Follow + Stabilizer off; show one-time hint card |
| Windows slide back after each head turn | Stabilizer on (smoothed 0DoF) fighting host transform | Same as above; detect via panel duty ≤40% |
| Desktop unusably huge/tiny on glasses | Glasses report no DPI | Apply Dextop density override on XR attach |
| Sensor stream dead after glasses OTA | Protocol changed across firmware | Version-gate control handshake; degrade to generic display, surface diagnostics |

